meta {
  name: Balance
  seq: 11
}

auth {
  mode: inherit
}

docs {
  The deposit of the site owner: `Order / Pay an order from the deposit` charges orders of the site from it. The API only reads it; it is topped up by a bank transfer against a bill, in the account of the site owner at https://store.4partners.io:

  1. Sign in as the site owner and fill in the company details at https://store.4partners.io/my/company: bills are issued to the company.
  2. At https://store.4partners.io/my/company/bill/list set the amount and the currency (`RUB`, `USD`, `EUR`) and download the bill as PDF.
  3. Pay the bill by bank transfer and mark it as paid in the same list.
  4. 4Partners credits the deposit when the money arrives: `Show the deposit` shows the new balance, and `List deposit operations` shows the credit with `type: adjustment`.

  Payments from your recipients go to your own payment provider; 4Partners gets only `deposit_due` from the deposit. Do not take a payment for an order of the site through the payment terminal of 4Partners: such a payment marks the order paid at its full price, and `Pay an order from the deposit` then gives 409 `order-already-paid`.
}
